'''Guinea-Bissau Sign Language''' ({{Langx|pt|Língua gestual guineense}} or {{Langx|pt|Língua de sinais guineense|label=none}}) is an incipient [[sign language]] evolving from the single school for the deaf in Guinea-Bissau, which was founded in [[Bissau]] in 2003. In 2005 a linguist and [[Portuguese Sign Language]] teacher found GBSL to still be basic, but with some consistency among students in the school and village use when the students went home.

It is not directly related to the Portuguese sign language, although it has borrowed the alphabet from it.<ref>{{Cite web |title=República da Guiné-Bissau (Republic of Guinea-Bissau) |url=https://africansignlanguagesresourcecenter.com/guine-bissau/ |access-date=2024-05-13 |website=African Sign Languages Resource Center |language=en-US}}</ref>

